src('SRC045','Echo Flight UFO incident not unique (Hastings article with partial transcripts of Salas 1996 and Hastings 2011 calls with Meiwald, and text of Meiwald 1 Oct 1996 letter)','Robert L. Hastings','ufohastings.com','posted c.2011','Advocacy article with partial transcripts and letter excerpt','SECONDARY','https://ufohastings.com/articles/echo-flight-ufo-incident-not-unique','','text read; audio not heard; letter image not viewed','%s'%A,'INC020;WIT012;EVD081;EVD082','Partial transcripts (edited: ums removed, "confidential comments" excluded at Meiwald request, audio hum). Letter given as an excerpt; says full letter is visible as an image.','Advocate-edited transcripts of real calls; best available text of Meiwald statements; not the original audio or letter.','PARTIALLY_VERIFIED','EXAMINED')
ev('EVD081',"Meiwald's own words (SRC045). 1996 call with Salas (Salas leads: 'some of our missiles started shutting down. Is that right?'): Meiwald 'Uh huh ... Right. We had security alarms and, uh ... problems at a couple of the, uh, sites.' He recalls two guards who went to an LF, lost radio contact on return, were 'scared to death', relieved of duty; 'they had seen these, some crazy things.' 1 Oct 1996 letter (excerpt): 'Our home site was Oscar'; topside security reported the mobile team saw a 'UFO' near an LF just east of Highway 19 (Grass Range to the Missouri); radio contact lost; 'Two very upset young men'; no personnel injury recalled; the crew 'formed ... Sept 66 in N [status]'. 2011 call with Hastings: recalls being woken, 'unusual indications on the consol', a security violation, team reporting 'unusual activity'; does NOT remember Salas telling him of a bright object at the gate; 'I'm saying I don't remember'; 'We had an incident in October [sic] Flight' (sic by Hastings); recalls missile count as six to eight per Hastings (not in transcript excerpt). So: Meiwald independently affirms Oscar and a team's UFO report at an outlying LF, assents (to a leading question) to missiles shutting down, and does not corroborate the gate object, the injured guard, or the number ten. The Salas gate-object and the Meiwald LF-object are separate reports (Salas, 9 May 2011 email: the second came to Meiwald from the FSC). No date, time, or bearing appears. This partly corrects EVD077/EVD078: Meiwald's letter excerpt alone (as quoted by Carlson) omitted missiles, but the 1996 call shows assent.",'TRANSCRIPT_COMPARISON','SRC045; SRC042','INC020;WIT012;EVD077;EVD078;CLM132','10002','CRITICAL','PARTIALLY_VERIFIED')
ev('EVD082',"Evaluation of Carlson's claim (SRC042) that nowhere does Meiwald link the event he describes with missile failures and that transcripts show nothing of the kind: partly wrong. In the 1996 call Meiwald says 'Uh huh' and 'Right' to the missile-shutdown sequence, though he supplies no detail and the question was leading. Carlson's other points stand: no UFO at the gate, no injury, no date, a minor security alert is a possible reading, the 'N' in Meiwald's letter is crew status and not necessarily a flight (Hastings brackets it as 'November Flight'; the origin of Salas's 'November' is not established from this).",'ANALYST_ASSESSMENT','SRC045;SRC042','CLM132;EXP039','10002','HIGH','PARTIALLY_VERIFIED')
